<title>GERMANY: German Heideldruck-Linotype deal approved.</title>
<headline>German Heideldruck-Linotype deal approved.</headline>
<dateline>HEIDELBERG, Germany 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's Heidelberger Druckmaschinen AG said on Wednesday the German Federal Cartel Office had approved its takeover of printing group Linotype-Hell AG.</p>
<p>It said that German bank Commerzbank would as a result sell its 79 percent stake in Linotype to Heideldruck, which manufactures printing equipment and is a subsidiary of electricity group Rheinelektra AG.</p>
<p>Linotype produces image setters and electronic colour systems.</p>
<p>Commerzbank had been holding the shares in anticipation of being able to sell them on to Heideldruck. The takeover was approved by Linotype shareholders in September.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
